    "body": "fix on issue/2583-machine-tree · PR #2747 · pinned by `machine_tree` suite (`every_shipped_machine_file_reads_as_a_tree`, `the_three_axis_vmc_keeps_its_parent_chain`, `the_tilt_head_puts_the_head_chain_on_the_tool_side`, `an_inch_file_scales_lengths_and_keeps_angles`, `a_malformed_tree_refuses_by_part_id_and_key`) · merges at the next cut\n\nTwo facts for the machine model (#2574):\n\n- `3axis-vmc.mch` is in the mirror form. It states no part tree and reads as an empty tree. The 3-axis chain is pinned on `vmc.mch`.\n- Most shipped 3-axis files put the `head` beside the axis chain. By the rule of this issue, all their axes read as table side. A correct model needs those files nested as the machine moves. The PR does not change a machine file.\n",
